# ── Infra / compose env (root .env) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored.
#
# This file carries ONLY the vars docker-compose substitutes (${...}) — the
# Postgres container credentials and the frontend's VITE_* mirrors. It is NOT
# loaded into the api/worker containers and is NOT read by the app's Settings.
# Application config (DATABASE_URL, AZURE_*, AUTH_DEV_BYPASS, …) lives in the
# separate app env file — see .env.app.example. The split lets Settings run with
# extra="forbid" (catch typo'd/stale keys) without these infra keys crashing it.

# ── Postgres container ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Consumed by the postgres service and to hand-build DATABASE_URL in compose.
# No app Settings fields exist for these — keep them out of the app env file.
# Left blank on purpose: never commit credentials, even local/mock ones. Set
# these in your gitignored .env — `scripts/setup.sh` fills them with a generated
# local-dev password on first run, or set your own.
POSTGRES_USER=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=

# ── OpenBao (secret store) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root token for the dev-mode vault that holds connection credentials (ADR 0039,
# replaces the plaintext RedisSecretStore). Compose substitutes it into both the
# openbao container (BAO_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN_ID) and the api/worker (OPENBAO_TOKEN),
# so the same value must also appear in .env.app — `scripts/setup.sh` generates
# it into both on first run.
#
# Blank on purpose: it is a credential, and none ship in tracked files. Compose
# fails loudly rather than starting an unreachable vault if it is unset.
OPENBAO_TOKEN=

# ── Sign-in mode — ONE switch for the whole compose stack (#1150) ─────────────
# The local stack boots into EMAIL ONE-TIME CODES (ADR 0032) against the bundled
# `mailpit` catcher: you type your address, DataQ mails a 6-digit code, and you
# read it in a web inbox at http://localhost:8025. No SMTP relay to bring, no real
# mailbox, nothing leaving this machine.
#
#   DATAQ_SIGNIN_EMAIL=you@example.com   → email sign-in, allow-listed to you
#   (key absent)                         → compose refuses to start and says why
#
# Developers only — the no-sign-in bypass (one fixed user, anyone who can reach
# the port is an admin). Off by default, never a fallback; both lines are needed:
#   DATAQ_SIGNIN_EMAIL=
#   DATAQ_DEV_BYPASS=true
#
# Deliberately COMMENTED OUT here, not blank: `scripts/setup.sh` asks for the
# address and writes the answer into your gitignored .env, and a blank line in
# this template would make it look answered and skip the question. An address is
# personal data — no tracked file carries one.
# DATAQ_SIGNIN_EMAIL=

# ── Frontend (Vite) auth mirrors ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite only exposes env vars prefixed VITE_ to client code. These mirror the
# backend AZURE_* vars so the SPA and the API agree on the tenant + client IDs.
# The bypass flag is derived from DATAQ_DEV_BYPASS above — there is no second
# switch to set. Substituted into the frontend service by compose.
VITE_AZURE_TENANT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_SPA_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_API_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_API_SCOPE=user_impersonation
